    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d976">

                <pb facs="0903" n="893" xml:id="pg893"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163/1119: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-08-20T17:00:00-04:00">August 20, 1941—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>516. Peiping’s despatch no. 43, June 21, 1941,<anchor n="60" xml:id="d976-f1"/>
                    reported Japanese trespass on American property at Tsining, Shantung, removal of
                    an American flag therefrom, and the looting thereof.</p>
                <p>The Department suggests that the Embassy place on record with the Foreign Office
                    our view that the Japanese Consul General’s reply of June 12, 1941 to the
                    American Vice Consul at Tsinan<anchor n="60" xml:id="d976-f2"/> is
                    unsatisfactory and request that the Foreign Office cause a further investigation
                    and report on the incident to be made.</p>
                <p>Sent to Tokyo via Shanghai. Repeated to Chungking and Peiping. Peiping please
                    forward code text to Tsinan by mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
